="https://www.darioamodei.com/essay/the-adolescence-of-technology">https://www.darioamodei.com/essay/the-adolescence-of-technology</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1292026">AI Links, 1/29/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.darioamodei.com/essay/the-adolescence-of-technology</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.darioamodei.com/essay/the-adolescence-of-technology</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2026 13:03:37 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colleges owe students a new learning contract]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>Adapted from keynote speech at the Association for Undergraduate Education in Research Universities, Jan 22, Washington DC…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://kathleendelaski.substack.com/p/colleges-owe-students-a-new-learning?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://kathleendelaski.substack.com/p/colleges-owe-students-a-new-learning?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/education-links-1302026">Education Links, 1/30/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://kathleendelaski.substack.com/p/colleges-owe-students-a-new-learning?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://kathleendelaski.substack.com/p/colleges-owe-students-a-new-learning?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Jan 2026 13:04:22 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Management as AI superpower]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>I just taught an experimental class at the University of Pennsylvania where I challenged students to create a startup from scratch in four days. Most of the people in the class were in the executive MBA program, so they were taking classes while also working as doctors, managers, or leaders in a variety of large and small companies. Few had ever coded. …</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/management-as-ai-superpower?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/management-as-ai-superpower?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1292026">AI Links, 1/29/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/management-as-ai-superpower?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.oneusefulthing.org/p/management-as-ai-superpower?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2026 13:03:37 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Claude Codes #3]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>We’re back with all the Claude that’s fit to Code. I continue to have great fun with it and find useful upgrades, but the biggest reminder is that you need the art to have an end other than itself. Don’t spend too long improving your setup, or especially improving how you improve your setup, without actually working on useful things…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://thezvi.substack.com/p/claude-codes-3?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://thezvi.substack.com/p/claude-codes-3?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1292026">AI Links, 1/29/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://thezvi.substack.com/p/claude-codes-3?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://thezvi.substack.com/p/claude-codes-3?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2026 13:03:37 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Discarding the Shaft-and-Belt Model of Software Development]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>It’s often been observed that taking full advantage of AI will require changing work practices, just as taking full advantage of electric motors in manufacturing required changing the way factories were laid out. But what will those changes look like? Early answers are starting to emerge, coming (unsurprisingly) from the field of software development. I…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://secondthoughts.ai/p/the-new-model-of-software-development?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://secondthoughts.ai/p/the-new-model-of-software-development?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/ai-links-1292026">AI Links, 1/29/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://secondthoughts.ai/p/the-new-model-of-software-development?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://secondthoughts.ai/p/the-new-model-of-software-development?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Jan 2026 13:03:37 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>